Here is the general guidance on outbuildings. A garden room usually does not need a planning application if it:

- is under 2.5 metres high,
- sits behind the front wall of the house,
- covers less than half of the garden.

Conservation areas and listed buildings are treated differently, so if 14 Mill Wynd is in either, you may need an application even if the room meets these limits.

